# python and the build systems written in it.
#
# meson is why these are here. kmod is configured with it, and so is most of
# what follows -- wayland, libdrm, pixman, libinput, mesa, wlroots, sway.
# Until now the host's meson ran and nobody noticed the image had none.
#
# meson installs through pip, so python has to be the chapter 8 one built
# with ensurepip rather than chapter 7's --without-ensurepip copy, and
# flit-core, packaging, wheel and setuptools are the build backends pip needs
# when it is told --no-build-isolation. ninja is meson's backend and is
# bootstrapped by python rather than built by meson, which is what keeps the
# two from being circular.
https://pypi.org/packages/source/f/flit-core/flit_core-3.12.0.tar.gz
https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/source/p/packaging/packaging-25.0.tar.gz
https://pypi.org/packages/source/w/wheel/wheel-0.46.1.tar.gz
https://pypi.org/packages/source/s/setuptools/setuptools-80.9.0.tar.gz
https://github.com/ninja-build/ninja/archive/v1.13.1/ninja-1.13.1.tar.gz
https://github.com/mesonbuild/meson/releases/download/1.8.3/meson-1.8.3.tar.gz

